      <h1 class="jr-h1">Collagen for Women: What Changes by Decade</h1>
      <p class="jr-standfirst">
        A woman's collagen does not decline in a straight line. It drifts through your late
        twenties, shifts in your thirties, and then falls off a ledge in the five years around
        menopause. Here is what actually changes at each stage, and what is worth doing about it.
      </p>

